{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428538-dread-power-ratings-and-claimed-rules","id":428538,"title":"Dread Power Ratings and Claimed Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-04T20:56:09-08:00","id":428538,"title":"Dread Power Ratings and Claimed Rules","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I looked through the Errata thread and it didn't seem to be the place for this sort of rules clarification so I made a separate post. If I'm wrong I apologize in advance.<br /> <br /> Edit here: removed Dread Power question from here.<br /> <br /> Also the Claimed Condition points us towards the list of Dread Powers without giving us suggestions on how many we should be assigning the Claimed. Is this an oversight? Or do the guidelines from Predators still apply and was simply not brought up to save on word-count? (For quick reference: 5 points of Dread Powers per point of Synthesis, Synthesis maxing out at Rank+1, with Synthesis increasing at a rate based on the Spirits Rank. [I did a word search and did find mention of Synthesis in the 4-Dot Rite Expel]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":4737,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","user":"Afro Luigi","date":".  Sniped by amechra on my Dread Powers question 03-05-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T03:05:12-08:00","id":428902,"title":"","content":"I didn't really have the wordcount to recreate a Synthesis-style system for Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> Claimed get as many Dread Powers as the Storyteller feels necessary for them. They explicitly do <i>not</i> use the old system, especially since I have only assigned dot ratings to those Dread Powers that actually have variable levels of effect (like natural weaponry) and then only to provide quick visual reference for the level that the creature has it as, not as a balancing cost or whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:39:02-08:00","id":432405,"title":"","content":"Which is a real shame, it would have been quite nice for building kitsune in second edition, pricing plug-ins for a cyberpunk werewolf game, or adding those dread powers to the list of those from hunter. <br /> <br /> Crossing my fingers for a later book to have the room for a more indepth look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:17:59-07:00","id":432439,"title":"","content":"To crosspost from a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428521-werewolf-2e-dread-powers\">similar thread</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428521-werewolf-2e-dread-powers?p=429075#post429075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there was no space for a Synthesis like system, I still think it is a shame to not give them dot ratings, especially as it is possible to include a rework of Synthesis in a future book. But of course it would then also be possible to allocate dot values to the old Dread Powers in that hypothetical book.<br /> <br /> We could always assign dot ratings ourselves to make it compatible with Hunter and the old rules.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Assigning dot ratings is at least something I am planning to do at some point, because I sometimes make Dread Powers available to players for 2 XP per dot (as priced according to Mortal Remains).</div> </div> </div> </div>But we should really confine this discussion to one of these two threads, or have one of the Moderators merge them (if that is possible).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}